  "ai_language_tip": "Use polite standard Russian (ru) everywhere in the region; in Kazakhstan and Kyrgyzstan Russian is the default business language in cities, while Kazakh/Kyrgyz may be preferred in some villages and state offices (kz, kg).",
  "english_ok": "rarely — Workable at large international hotels and some upscale Moscow/St Petersburg restaurants; very limited at clinics, garages, taxis and state offices.",
  "politeness": "Formal 'Вы' with strangers; open with 'Здравствуйте' and say on whose behalf you call; first name + patronymic is the respectful address for older staff; close with 'Спасибо, до свидания'. Tone is brisk and businesslike.",
  "name_tip": "Bookings go 'на фамилию …' (surname); surnames change by gender (-ов/-ова, -ин/-ина), so give the exact form; spell Latin names letter by letter and expect Cyrillic transcription.",
  "phone_tip": "Russia/Kazakhstan mobile +7 9xx / +7 7xx, domestically dialled with 8 (e.g. 8 9XX 12345678); Kyrgyzstan +996 then 9 digits; confirmations by SMS, MAX or Telegram in Russia, WhatsApp in kz and kg.",
  "time_tip": "24-hour clock is standard in writing; speech often uses 'в половине восьмого' = 7:30 (half OF the eighth hour, like German) and 'без пятнадцати восемь' = 7:45; always read back as 24h ('в девятнадцать тридцать').",
  "number_tip": "Phone digits are read in 3-3-2-2 groups as whole numbers (hundreds, then tens), so read back group by group; party size often uses collective numerals ('нас трое', 'на двоих').",
  "avoid_calling": "Avoid lunch 13:00–14:00 at clinics and offices, restaurant peaks 13:00 and 19:00–21:00, and calls after 21:00; long New Year holidays (1–8 January) slow everything.",
  "closed_days": "Shops, salons and restaurants usually open 7 days; state offices and many private clinics close Sunday or work short Saturday; national holidays 1–8 January, 23 February, 8 March, 1 and 9 May, 12 June, 4 November (ru); kz and kg have their own holiday calendars incl. Nauryz in March.",
  "booking_channels": "Yandex Maps online table booking and Restoclub for restaurants; Gosuslugi/EMIAS (Moscow) for public polyclinics and ProDoctorov or SberHealth for private doctors; YCLIENTS-style online booking for salons; Yandex Eda and marketplace apps for delivery (Delivery Club closed in 2023); phone still common for small businesses; in kz Kaspi and 2GIS are widely used.",
  "voice_menu": "Public polyclinics, Moscow 122 health line, banks, mobile operators (MTS, Beeline, MegaFon, T2 (ex-Tele2)) and Russian Post use IVR or voice robots; small restaurants and salons answer directly.",
  "callback_habits": "Platforms send SMS confirmation; Yandex 'по заявке' bookings need a confirming call from the restaurant; clinics send SMS reminders; small businesses confirm by SMS, Telegram or the domestic MAX messenger in Russia (WhatsApp blocked in Russia since February 2026, Telegram throttled), and by WhatsApp in kz and kg.",
